From 8b17c42d7f804d8409bc1ad2ddf3e3699b675815 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:22:14 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(2d): turn a contour seam lead only when it crosses its
 own ring

On a round-cornered outside plate, the ring's seam falls on a fitted
corner arc. A linear lead along that arc's end tangent crossed the ring
next to the seam, and verify held the post on each level, with tabs or
without.

A new seam_tangents (lead_seam.rs) checks the full lead at a closed
ring's seam against the ring's own feeds, by the verifier's crossing
law. Only a crossing lead is mirrored across the other end's tangent,
and only if the mirror does not cross. Every other ring keeps its
tangents, so the #3053 regression (#3111: a moved seam and a reversed
vertical entry arc on a plain rectangle) does not come back.

Fixes #3019

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
